  "name": "Tempus",
  "editorial_article": "'Tempus' is a studio album by the Scottish Celtic rock band Skerryvore, released in April 2023. This project marked a significant moment in the band's long-standing career, showcasing their evolution from traditional roots into a more expansive, contemporary sound that leans heavily into pop, rock, and anthemic production. As the title suggests—'tempus' being the Latin word for 'time'—the record serves as a reflective look at the passage of years, capturing both the intimacy of the band's acoustic heritage and their ambition for larger, global stages. \n\nProduced with a polished, arena-ready sensibility, the album features soaring melodies, intricate arrangements of traditional instruments like the fiddle and bagpipes blended with electric guitars and driving percussion. Tracks on the project are designed to evoke both nostalgia and hope, resonating with the group's dedicated fanbase while reaching for new listeners through its accessible song structures. By bridging the gap between Scotland's storied folk history and modern radio-friendly production, 'Tempus' stands as a definitive representation of Skerryvore's ability to maintain their cultural identity while embracing stylistic growth. The album was widely received as a testament to the group's endurance and their continued relevance in the contemporary folk-rock landscape.",
